Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:44:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1411/1463] HERESY 1458: the LoRA section finished: the wave's
 grid in minutes and seconds, the song's end, Shift onto the grid; the picker
 over the page up to 1800 px; what the budget lets run
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor 15.10.2026, after the duduk's wave («Волна реально работает»): «Не хватает ещё более чёткой сетки в бекграунд редактирования графика… поле для ввода примерного расчётного по длительности трека генерируемого. Выставлять по этому числу минут и секунд сетку в графе волны»; «Редактирование параметров с волной адаптеров можно так же в full screen по кнопке — как у меня с редактором лирики. На 1800px»; «Твоё предложение принимаю по показу более точных долей применения в выхлопе». The wave's graph is drawn at its own size in pixels (190 px in the form, up to 440 over the page; round points, one-pixel lines), with a grid of the strength's quarters and twentieths and of minutes and seconds along the length the engine runs the wave over: Output's length (the request's duration caps the music half's frames and the sound half's span follows, pipeline.h), not the song's own. «Song ≈» (m:ss, 3.5 or seconds; kept as yue2.loraSongLen) marks the song's expected end with a dashed line and dims what lies past it; longer than Output's length, a word says the song stops there. A read-out says where the pointer stands; Shift lands a point on the grid. The button beside the LoRAs' name lifts the picker over the page, up to 1800 px wide (as the lyrics go over it, 1169); ⤡, Esc or a click beside it puts it back, and so does another room. With a budget, a strength that gives way shows what runs, counted as lora-rt.h counts it at the waves' top (in order: served from the top row; shared: in proportion; capped at the red line): its number amber, its road dimmed past a tick, its tip saying why; Music, together and Sound, together show what runs of what is asked and are amber, not red, when the budget holds them (the same sum in both modes; the rows differ). Six new strings in all eleven catalogs. Kitchen suite 817/0 (three new checks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
